WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:59.180
[Music]

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:03.700
[Narrator:] In recent years, we have made
important progress towards the final conquest

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.890
of tuberculosis, to a great extent aided by
newer and better hospitals and sanatoriums,

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:14.780
and naturally, as every health officer knows, such a hospital or sanatorium is the best

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.530
place to treat tuberculosis when it is possible.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:23.050
With their elaborate equipment, constant and
thorough supervision and complete facilities,

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:26.310
these hospitals help patients to conquer their
disease.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:31.410
They give more effective help because they
can apply definite principles of 

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:37.619
isolation, treatment, education and rehabilitation.

00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:41.590
Every nurse has had some glimpse of these
principles at work during her professional

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:47.330
training and experience. The first element
of tuberculosis care is the understanding

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.459
between doctor and nurse.

00:01:49.459 --> 00:01:54.459
This understanding is vital to successful
collaboration in the care of the patient.

00:01:54.459 --> 00:02:00.450
It is also vital to the relationship of the
nurse to the patient and family; always the

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:08.350
doctor is responsible for making the diagnosis. The doctor also orders medication and plans treatment.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:13.709
The nurse is responsible for administering
the doctor's plan. She shares with the doctor

00:02:13.709 --> 00:02:17.640
a responsibility for teaching patients and
families.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:23.750
Seldom can we equal at any home the effectiveness
of hospital care, but we can apply a number

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:29.290
of the same definite principles which are
familiar elements in contagious disease nursing technique.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:35.299
In the scenes which follow, you'll see a typical
family and a typical case for the public health

00:02:35.299 --> 00:02:40.129
nursing compared to hospital nursing. There
are both similarities and differences in this

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:44.319
case from the time the doctor in charge calls
upon the public health nurse.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:49.560
[Doctor:] Mrs. Abbott, this is Dr. Caneaux.
I have another patient for you; the name is

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:54.129
Evans. He has a wife and has two children.

00:02:54.129 --> 00:03:01.099
The involvement is bilateral. The sputum is
positive. The family will need your usual

00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:04.510
instruction. Will you meet me there at 11,
please?

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:11.510
[Mrs. Abbott:] 11 o'clock, yes. Yes, I know.
I'll see you then, doctor.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.390
[Narrator:] Like the nurse in the hospital,
this public health nurse will follow the doctor's

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:22.189
orders for treatment, but she must also pass
on the responsibility for daily care to the family.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:27.569
Following the doctor's orders, she will help
him to explain the treatment to the family

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:32.790
and will teach some responsible member to
follow the routine of care required for the

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.999
patient's welfare and for their own safety.

00:03:34.999 --> 00:03:40.989
You'll see brief examples of teaching by this
nurse. Keep in mind as you watch them that

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:46.239
she has carried over to public health service
from her hospital training five proven elements

00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:48.239
of teaching which you will see are used.

00:03:48.239 --> 00:03:55.239
Here they are, principles of teaching that
are applied in all effective education. First,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:04.840
good hospital teaching is affirmative. The
teacher must make far less use of don't than

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.030
of do.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:14.030
Second, the item to be taught must be stated
clearly in a few simple words. Keep instruction

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:16.639
short.

00:04:16.639 --> 00:04:23.280
Third, the teacher must demonstrate what she
has described.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:30.280
Fourth, the learner must demonstrate that
he fully understands the instruction.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:38.080
Finally, use printed material as a reminder
of your teaching. Get it from your health

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.539
department or Tuberculosis Association.

00:04:41.539 --> 00:04:46.280
Printed material can never take the place
of person-to-person teaching, any more than

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:51.180
a short motion picture can teach complete
home nursing, but it can help make your teaching

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:57.400
more effective by crystallizing the details
of treatment. But, when it comes to such a

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:03.699
problem as the patient's morale, printed material is of little use. That factor must be governed

00:05:03.699 --> 00:05:06.580
only by the human approach.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:11.020
This element of morale is so important that
even before teaching this family the routine

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:16.780
of care, and before showing the patient how to protect his family, the nurse tries to establish

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.220
the right attitude in the patient's mind.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:25.139
She chooses her words and her approach carefully,
explaining simply, trying to install the will

00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:30.370
to recover. She makes it clear that treatment
is not just something we do to the patient

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:33.340
but something to which he must contribute.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:38.550
The patient's morale is one of the determining
factors in his recovery, and it controls the

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:43.430
extent of the protection he gives the family.
With the understanding and cooperation of

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:48.580
the patient, the nurse's work will be more
successful. She must make him believe it is

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.699
worthwhile to get well.

00:05:50.699 --> 00:05:56.220
The next treatment principle to be transferred
from hospital to home is separation of the

00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:01.069
patient from the community. This can best
be done when we remove the patient to a 

00:06:01.069 --> 00:06:03.879
tuberculosis hospital or sanatorium.

00:06:03.879 --> 00:06:10.879
In a well-conducted hospital, separation from
a community is combined with evidence that

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:17.220
treatment is conducted for the patient's own
benefit and protection.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:21.979
In the home, we must apply whatever we can
of communicable disease nursing technique.

00:06:21.979 --> 00:06:26.330
When possible, we try to assign the patient
to a single, private room.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:31.849
In any case, a separate bed is essential and
the patient must have completely separate

00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:37.199
equipment as well. Dishes, linens and personal
needs should be kept apart.

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:43.449
The nurse explains this affirmatively as routine
medical procedure without overemphasizing

00:06:43.449 --> 00:06:48.259
the isolation of the patient. She persuades
the patient and family that separation will

00:06:48.259 --> 00:06:51.979
protect the patient as well as protect others
from his bacilli.

00:06:51.979 --> 00:06:58.569
She keeps a safety zone as wide as possible.
Now she improvises visible barriers to symbolize

00:06:58.569 --> 00:07:04.169
the privacy of her patient even in a one-room
dwelling. Naturally it is important to protect

00:07:04.169 --> 00:07:08.680
others from the tuberculosis bacilli, which
invades every corner of the room.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:14.610
These paratroopers can carry tuberculosis
from patient to family, but their near relatives

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:20.720
carry colds and pneumonia from family to patient,
too. So a relative's cold can complicate

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:25.379
your patient's illness dangerously.

00:07:25.379 --> 00:07:29.620
After this is explained clearly to the patient
and family, the nurse leaves this printed

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:36.270
remind. The public health nurse has been hailed
as a shoe-leather epidemiologist. Her teaching

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:40.430
about infection provides a natural introduction
to this part of her service, 

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.400
checking the patient's contacts.

00:07:42.409 --> 00:07:47.960
Here's a positive method of identifying all
contacts, which has helped to find a lot of tuberculosis.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:58.360
There represented by the square you have the
patient, a circle for the wife, a line of

00:07:58.849 --> 00:08:05.289
descent and the two children. Shade the square
for a known, active case.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:12.280
Put a question mark for each known contact.
Does the patient have any brothers or sisters?

00:08:12.879 --> 00:08:19.530
Show them. And here's your carrier, a sister
who died of tuberculosis.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:26.530
The system is simple. Modify the basic idea
and it'll fit any family condition.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:33.349
It's an effective aid in finding cases early enough to make treatment successful.

00:08:33.349 --> 00:08:38.429
Now we come to our next factor of treatment;
cleanliness.

00:08:38.429 --> 00:08:42.540
Simple cleanliness helps to fight tuberculosis.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:49.550
We cannot duplicate in the home complete hospital
apparatus, but we can teach the value and

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:57.050
importance of cleanliness. No case is so primitive
that soap and water cannot be used.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:02.830
As a supplement to soap and water, explain
the cleansing properties of sunlight affirmably

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:07.200
to the family. Teach the family that cleanliness
helps to protect everybody.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:13.010
That they as well as the patient guard themselves
by practicing cleanliness. Make the family

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:18.020
understand how cleanliness, particularly with
dishes and other objects used by the patient,

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:23.840
is a fundamental necessity and teach the patient, too, that his cleanliness will protect the

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:29.850
family. He must learn to do his part to prevent
further infection of himself and others.

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:34.330
The use of disposable tissues must be made
perfectly clear to the patient. The whole

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:40.450
family must understand how to handle such
contaminated material. This type of instruction

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:46.230
shows very plainly the steps an effective
teaching as they apply in the home care of

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.030
tuberculosis.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:54.200
Watch now the application of these elements
as we explain the disposal of contaminated

00:09:54.200 --> 00:10:01.200
tissues to the family. First, explanation.
Then, demonstration. Show the whole procedure.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:12.660
Then you get participation by having the procedure
carried out for you.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:22.640
Now explanation, demonstration, and participation
are repeated in stressing the second point

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:28.120
in the procedure that the family must guard
themselves, too, by constant cleanliness, here

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:35.120
shown by washing the hands thoroughly after
handling contaminated material.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:46.080
And, finally now the printed reminder covers
both points in the procedure.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:52.370
We have purposely delayed the vital fifth
principle of treatment which is rest, but

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:58.280
we need a foundation upon which rest will
be possible and effective.

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:05.280
Notice how the principles of treatment form
a pyramid. Confidence in medical direction

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:12.690
is essential in all treatment. Rest is little
more than a word until we establish the opportunity

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:16.020
of complete separation and privacy.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:23.020
A clean bed and a clean body are great helps
in relaxation and rest. Remember, the family

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:32.110
has never seen bed rest in a tuberculosis
hospital. You must explain it to them.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:39.970
Bed rest means being washed and bathed and
shaved in bed. Bed rest means, too, being

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:44.690
fed in bed; not getting up for any reason.

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:51.070
And most important, bed rest means a recumbent
position not sitting up until the doctor prescribes that change.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:59.380
Finally, bed rest means regular,
daily intervals of complete relaxation;

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.700
rest for both body and mind.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:08.700
The patient may shorten his illness by giving
hours each day to absolute bed rest.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:16.500
And it is necessary to explain gently, firmly to the family and to friends, that listening to others

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.270
is not rest.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:26.030
The next important item is nutrition; not
only what to eat but the balance of meals.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:32.190
Talk in terms of a common sense menu which
can be purchased by the patient's family with

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:38.820
the funds available. The question of nutrition
may well be taken up in the instruction

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:39.820
of the second visit.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:45.880
In a fresh, sterile gown, the nurse teaches
the family to avoid any contamination of the

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:50.950
food supply. In planning a diet, assure the
family that the patient makes little real

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:56.650
gain by being stuffed and that weight alone
does not mean recovery.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:03.140
Show the family how to improvise a tray and
how to make the food on that tray look attractive.

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:08.470
The result will help to stimulate the patient's
appetite and his intake of the right foods

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:15.470
for his needs. Yes, even a meal that's good
for you can be appetizing.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:27.580
Suitable recreation when medically approved
is an important factor in inducing patients

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:32.750
to accept treatment whether in the hospital
or in the home.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:39.750
Your instruction to the family is not complete
unless you yourself have given some thought,

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:47.420
and provoke in the home some thought, as to
what the patient may do for recreation during

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:52.700
his illness, especially when he becomes sputum
negative.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:58.710
Now here is an example of hand work learned
from an occupational therapist and taught

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:03.950
to the patient under the doctor's approval.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:14.100
As the patient continues to make progress,
his reading time may be gradually increased

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:18.900
and now with his recovery approaching, the
public health nurse arranges for a conference.

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:22.890
[Mrs. Abbott:] Doctor, I came to see if the
patient is ready for rehabilitation training.

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:25.410
Mr. Bronson is from the state agency.

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:30.600
[Doctor:] Yes, he should be ready to start
on Mr. Bronson's plan the first of next month.

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:34.880
[Mr. Bronson:] Figuring on three month's training,
can we put him on a job when it's completed?

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:39.480
[Doctor:] I believe we can count on that.
Send him in for a re-check regularly while

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:44.980
he is training. If all continues to go well,
the physical demands you describe here will

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:48.380
be well within his tolerance.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:52.200
[Mrs. Abbott:] Thank you, doctor.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:15:00.220
[ Background music ]

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:05.100
[Narrator:] Yes, here is our ultimate goal,
the final reward for patient effort, care

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:08.980
and thought: to get the patient back on his
feet.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:14.030
Back to a job suitable to his condition and
the future needs of his family, to make him

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:18.660
a working, contributing member of the community.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:21.120
[Background music]

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:28.120
You may obtain printed material for the instruction
of patient of the family from the agency that

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:31.130
arranged for the showing of this film.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:37.110
Make yourself familiar with all of the publications
available from your local Tuberculosis Association.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:56.700
[ Background music ]

